.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt RG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rg
.Nd search files for lines that match a regular expression
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar pattern
.Op Ar path ...
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Fl -files
.Op Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm ,
ripgrep, searches each
.Ar path ,
or the current directory, recursively, for lines that match
.Ar pattern ,
a regular expression, and prints each with the name of its file.
It skips the files and directories that
.Pa .gitignore ,
.Pa .ignore
and
.Pa .rgignore
files name, hidden files and directories, and binary files;
.Fl u
searches the ignored files as well,
.Fl uu
the hidden ones too, and
.Fl uuu
binary files besides.
Its own regular expressions run in time linear in the input and have no
back-references or look-around;
.Fl P
uses PCRE2 instead, which has both.
.Ql rg --files
lists the files it would search.
.Ql rg -h
gives a summary of the options and
.Ql rg --help
describes each.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root has
.Nm
when it is built with the agents layer:
.Ql make ARCH=x86_64 GNU_AGENTS=ripgrep os-real-gnu-ext2 ,
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all ,
which the release to the installed machine uses.
The program is the author's own build of version 15.2.0, a static Rust
executable for musl with PCRE2 built in, installed unmodified as the release
has it.
.Pa /opt/ripgrep/rg
is the program, and
.Pa /usr/bin/rg
and
.Pa /bin/rg
link to it.
ripgrep is under the MIT license or the Unlicense, at the user's choice:
.Pa /opt/ripgrep/COPYING
says so, beside
.Pa LICENSE-MIT
and
.Pa UNLICENSE .
The release's own manual page,
.Pa /opt/ripgrep/doc/rg.1 ,
has the same text as
.Ql rg --help ;
.Xr man 1
does not read it.
Completions for bash, fish and zsh are in
.Pa /opt/ripgrep/complete ,
and no shell loads them.
.Pp
.Nm
reads no configuration file unless
.Ev RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH
names one: a file with one argument on each line, which comes before those
of the command line.
It chooses how many threads to search with from the number of processors
it may run on, unless
.Fl j
gives the number.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH
the configuration file
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /opt/ripgrep/rg
the program
.It Pa /opt/ripgrep/COPYING
its license, with
.Pa LICENSE-MIT
and
.Pa UNLICENSE
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when a line matched and no error occurred, 1 when no line matched, and 2
on an error, unless
.Fl q
was given and a line matched.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print, with their line numbers, the lines of the C sources under the
current directory that have the word
.Ql main :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ rg -n -w -t c main
.Ed
.Pp
List the shell scripts of a tree, the ignored ones too:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ rg -u --files -g '*.sh'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr grep 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/blob/15.2.0/GUIDE.md "The ripgrep user guide"
